// Axis delta: type .display — a serif headline over a sans body — the editorial pairing.
//
// Mood-INdependent: a typeface is not solved against a ground the way a hue
// is, so one file serves every palette.
//
// `l0_display_family` is separate from `l0_family` on purpose. A serif
// headline over a sans body is the commonest pairing in the corpus, and a
// single family token cannot say it — which is why `serif_display` and
// `font_pair` were counted as two gaps and are answered by one axis.
let l0_family         = "sans"
let l0_display_family = "serif"
let l0_tracking       = 0
